---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site'
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility" description="How this site is built to be usable by everyone.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p>
      <h1>Accessibility statement</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        This site aims to meet WCAG 2.1 Level AA. It is built for children, families, and
        educators, so it should work on a phone, with a keyboard, and with a screen reader.
      </p>

      <h2>What we have done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Semantic landmarks and one clear heading structure per page.</li>
        <li>A skip-to-content link as the first focusable element.</li>
        <li>Keyboard access throughout, including the mobile menu, which announces whether it is expanded.</li>
        <li>Visible focus indicators on every interactive element.</li>
        <li>Text and interface colors checked for contrast against their backgrounds.</li>
        <li>Meaningful alt text on images; decorative artwork is hidden from screen readers.</li>
        <li>Support for reduced-motion preferences.</li>
        <li>No autoplaying audio or video, and no information conveyed by color alone.</li>
        <li>Storybook PDFs are always available as a plain download link, not only through an embedded viewer.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Storybooks are published as PDFs produced during workshop sessions. These are image-based
          and are not screen-reader accessible. If you need a book in another format, please ask.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Telling us about a problem</h2>
      <p>
        If something on this site is hard to use, contact{' '}
        <a href={siteConfig.parentOrg.url} rel="noopener">{siteConfig.parentOrg.name}</a>. We want
        to know.
      </p>

      <div class="note">
        <p>
          <strong>Note for the project team.</strong> Add a direct contact address here before
          publishing, and re-check this page after any design change.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .note {
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-lavender-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .note p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
